# Planar clang-tidy configuration — adopted from tabula (D16), corrected at
# task 6438. Identifier naming only, for now — lower_case identifiers, `_`
# private/protected member prefix, and tabula's deliberate exception kept:
# template parameters are CamelCase, the one non-lower_case identifier kind,
# kept as the visual signal distinguishing a template parameter from a
# concrete type. Use the pinned LLVM's clang-tidy (docs/toolchain-parity.md).
#
# Task 6438 removed tabula's `_` PublicMemberSuffix rule: it never matched
# this codebase's actual convention (CLAUDE.md § C++ Style: plain snake_case
# throughout, e.g. `struct parsed_args`) and was firing on 2925 of 3030
# measured warnings (96.5%) — a config/codebase disagreement inherited
# wholesale from tabula rather than a real defect. Public members now fall
# back to VariableCase (lower_case), matching what the codebase already
# does almost everywhere (see e.g. src/engine/identity/scope.cppm).
---
Checks: >
  -*,
  readability-identifier-naming
CheckOptions:
  # LEADING underscore on private/protected data members: `_timeout`, never
  # `timeout_`. OPERATOR-DECIDED at task 6577, and the codebase was brought
  # to it in the same change (17 members across 7 files renamed).
  #
  # This rule arrived from tabula at M0 (decision D16) and, being advisory,
  # never gated anything — so the M1/M3/M4 engine ports were written against
  # it in the trailing style while the later cmd/ext ports happened to match
  # it, and `lib/db/db.cppm` ended up carrying both. The rule is unchanged;
  # what changed is that the code now agrees with it and CLAUDE.md § C++
  # Style states it, so the next reader does not have to infer it.
  #
  # Public members — including every field of a plain `struct`, which is most
  # of this codebase — are bare snake_case and fall through to VariableCase.
  # Task 6438 removed tabula's PublicMemberSuffix rule for exactly that
  # reason; do not reintroduce a suffix rule here.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix
    value: '_'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberPrefix
    value: '_'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.StructCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase
    value: lower_case
  # Template parameters are PascalCase (D16) — deliberately the one
  # un-lower_case identifier kind, so it stays the sole signal that
  # distinguishes a template parameter from a concrete type at point of use.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TemplateParameterCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TypeTemplateParameterCase
    value: CamelCase

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Task 6439: two conventions this codebase holds DELIBERATELY, which
  # `lower_case` rejects categorically. Both were measured, not assumed —
  # together they were 111 of the 114 distinct findings (97%), the same
  # config/codebase disagreement shape task 6438 found in the inherited
  # `PublicMemberSuffix` rule. Renaming to satisfy the rule would make the
  # code worse in both cases.
  #
  # 1. `L` — the Lua C API's universal name for `lua_State*`. 48 findings,
  #    all in engine/execute/host.cpp. Every Lua binding and every page of
  #    upstream Lua documentation calls it `L`; `l` would break that
  #    recognizability for a naming rule's benefit.
  #
  # 2. A TRAILING UNDERSCORE, which here is FORCED rather than chosen.
  #    `namespace import_ = engine::local::import_;` exists because
  #    `import` is a C++20 keyword and cannot name a namespace. `is_`,
  #    `profile_`, `run_`, `tier_`, `code_`, `error_` and friends
  #    disambiguate an alias, parameter or member against a type or member
  #    of the same name. The pattern is anchored (`..._$`) so it permits a
  #    trailing underscore and nothing else — a leading underscore stays a
  #    private/protected member per the Prefix rules above, and a DOUBLE
  #    underscore anywhere stays an error, which is correct: it is reserved
  #    to the implementation by [lex.name]/3. Three such variables were
  #    real defects and were renamed in this same change.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ParameterIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^(L|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+)*_)$'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.VariableIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^(L|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+)*_)$'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+)*_$'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+)*_$'
...
